{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 649 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "55e9e0c0000f6cf207b7e559707ec99700b3541582d17d8d41502dd679567861" :edb/db-before-t 648 :edb/db-after-t 649 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533961 50 #inst "2026-10-05T17:48:12.962Z" 13194139533961 true] [17592186059735 1020 #edb/ref 17592186269014 13194139533961 true] [17592186059735 1020 #edb/ref 17592186269018 13194139533961 true] [17592186059735 1020 #edb/ref 17592186269035 13194139533961 true] [17592186059735 1020 #edb/ref 17592186269052 13194139533961 true] [17592186059736 1020 #edb/ref 17592186268997 13194139533961 true] [17592186059736 1020 #edb/ref 17592186269004 13194139533961 true] [17592186059736 1020 #edb/ref 17592186269011 13194139533961 true] [17592186059736 1020 #edb/ref 17592186269021 13194139533961 true] [17592186059736 1020 #edb/ref 17592186269038 13194139533961 true] [17592186059741 1020 #edb/ref 17592186268990 13194139533961 true] [17592186059741 1020 #edb/ref 17592186269024 13194139533961 true] [17592186059741 1020 #edb/ref 17592186269028 13194139533961 true] [17592186059741 1020 #edb/ref 17592186269031 13194139533961 true] [17592186059741 1020 #edb/ref 17592186269045 13194139533961 true] [17592186060171 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533961 true] [17592186060171 1145 "The range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nNote that the angle $\\theta $ spans the first and second quadrants.\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ is negative, our answer is an angle that lies in the second quadrant, where cosine is negative.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964047/assets/dbf36192ac332dc49ed75278838e989a37ac7d888311be1b8b059a7b59667aa6.png)\n\nFrom the values in the second quadrant, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{4})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})=\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.\n$$" 13194139533961 true] [17592186268990 1017 #edb/ref 17592186268991 13194139533961 true] [17592186268990 1089 "q-117411" 13194139533961 true] [17592186268990 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533961 true] [17592186268990 1100 "$-6\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})=$" 13194139533961 true] [17592186268990 1113 #uuid "02c3cce7-ac66-5194-ad1f-3ef5e81a3aa2" 13194139533961 true] [17592186268990 1145 "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's take a look at the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964047/assets/a33ea7c6d1aa7cd7e54376aefb2af4347da59a61ecaabdbf4964d41b9661870a.png)\n\nFrom the values in the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{11\\pi }{6})=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHowever, $\\frac{11\\pi }{6}$ does not lie within the range of $\\theta .$ To get an angle that's coterminal with $\\frac{11\\pi }{6}$ that lies within the range of $\\theta ,$ we subtract $2\\pi .$\n\n$$\n\\frac{11\\pi }{6}-2\\pi =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2}) & =(-6)\\cdot (-\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533961 true] [17592186268991 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268992 13194139533961 true] [17592186268991 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268993 13194139533961 true] [17592186268991 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268994 13194139533961 true] [17592186268991 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268995 13194139533961 true] [17592186268991 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268996 13194139533961 true] [17592186268991 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533961 true] [17592186268991 1041 "selection" 13194139533961 true] [17592186268991 1104 #edb/ref 17592186268995 13194139533961 true] [17592186268991 1110 #uuid "132d2a0e-ea20-5019-adc4-612fc73aac64" 13194139533961 true] [17592186268992 1034 "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" 1319